						"description": "# Create Customer API\n\nThis endpoint allows you to create a new customer in the system. It accepts a POST request with customer details in the request body.\n\n## Purpose\n\nThe purpose of this API is to register a new customer by providing their name and email address.\n\n## Request\n\n### URL\n\n`{{baseUrl}}/customers`\n\n### Method\n\n`POST`\n\n### Request Body\n\nThe request body must be in JSON format and should include the following parameters:\n\n- **name** (string): The full name of the customer.\n    \n- **email** (string): The email address of the customer.\n    \n\n#### Example Request\n\n``` json\n{\n  \"name\": \"John Doe\",\n  \"email\": \"john.doe@example.com\"\n}\n\n ```\n\n## Expected Responses\n\nUpon successful creation of a customer, the API will return a JSON object containing the following fields:\n\n- **customerId** (string): A unique identifier for the newly created customer.\n    \n- **name** (string): The name of the customer.\n    \n- **email** (string): The email address of the customer.\n    \n\n### Example Response\n\n``` json\n{\n  \"customerId\": \"12345\",\n  \"name\": \"John Doe\",\n  \"email\": \"john.doe@example.com\"\n}\n\n ```\n\n## Important Notes and Best Practices\n\n- Ensure that the email provided is valid and unique to avoid conflicts.\n    \n- Always validate the input data before sending the request to minimize errors.\n    \n- Handle responses appropriately, especially error responses, to inform users of any issues with their request.\n    \n- Utilize Postman's features such as environments and collections to streamline your API testing process.\n    \n\nThis endpoint allows you to create a new customer in the system. It accepts a POST request with customer details in the request body.\n\n## Purpose\n\nThe purpose of this API is to register a new customer by providing their name and email address.\n\n## How to Use\n\n1. **Endpoint**: Send a POST request to `{{baseUrl}}/customers`.\n    \n2. **Headers**: Ensure that the `Content-Type` header is set to `application/json`.\n    \n3. **Request Body**: Include the customer details in the request body in JSON format.\n    \n\n## Request\n\n### URL\n\n`{{baseUrl}}/customers`\n\n### Method\n\n`POST`\n\n### Request Body\n\nThe request body must be in JSON format and should include the following parameters:\n\n- **name** (string): The full name of the customer.\n    \n- **email** (string): The email address of the customer.\n    \n\n#### Example Request\n\n``` json\n{\n  \"name\": \"John Doe\",\n  \"email\": \"john.doe@example.com\"\n}\n\n ```\n\n## Expected Responses\n\nUpon successful creation of a customer, the API will return a JSON object containing the following fields:\n\n- **customerId** (string): A unique identifier for the newly created customer.\n    \n- **name** (string): The name of the customer.\n    \n- **email** (string): The email address of the customer.\n    \n\n### Example Response\n\n``` json\n{\n  \"customerId\": \"12345\",\n  \"name\": \"John Doe\",\n  \"email\": \"john.doe@example.com\"\n}\n\n ```\n\n## Important Notes and Best Practices\n\n- Ensure that the email provided is valid and unique to avoid conflicts.\n    \n- Always validate the input data before sending the request to minimize errors.\n    \n- Handle responses appropriately, especially error responses, to inform users of any issues with their request.\n    \n\nThis endpoint allows you to create a new customer in the system. It accepts a POST request with customer details in the request body.\n\n## Request\n\n### URL\n\n`{{baseUrl}}/customers`\n\n### Method\n\n`POST`\n\n### Request Body\n\nThe request body must be in JSON format and should include the following parameters:\n\n- **name** (string): The full name of the customer.\n    \n- **email** (string): The email address of the customer.\n    \n\n#### Example Request\n\n``` json\n{\n  \"name\": \"John Doe\",\n  \"email\": \"john.doe@example.com\"\n}\n\n ```\n\n## Response\n\nUpon successful creation of a customer, the API will return a JSON object containing the following fields:\n\n- **customerId** (string): A unique identifier for the newly created customer.\n    \n- **name** (string): The name of the customer.\n    \n- **email** (string): The email address of the customer.\n    \n\n### Example Response\n\n``` json\n{\n  \"customerId\": \"12345\",\n  \"name\": \"John Doe\",\n  \"email\": \"john.doe@example.com\"\n}\n\n ```\n\nThis endpoint allows you to create a new customer in the system. It accepts a POST request with customer details in the request body.\n\n## Request\n\n### URL\n\n`{{baseUrl}}/customers`\n\n### Method\n\n`POST`\n\n### Request Body\n\nThe request body must be in JSON format and should include the following parameters:\n\n- **name** (string): The full name of the customer.\n    \n- **email** (string): The email address of the customer.\n    \n\n#### Example Request\n\n``` json\n{\n  \"name\": \"John Doe\",\n  \"email\": \"john.doe@example.com\"\n}\n\n ```\n\n## Response\n\nUpon successful creation of a customer, the API will return a JSON object containing the following fields:\n\n- **customerId** (string): A unique identifier for the newly created customer.\n    \n- **name** (string): The name of the customer.\n    \n- **email** (string): The email address of the customer.\n    \n\n### Example Response\n\n``` json\n{\n  \"customerId\": \"12345\",\n  \"name\": \"John Doe\",\n  \"email\": \"john.doe@example.com\"\n}\n\n ```\n\n## Request\n\n### URL\n\n`{{baseUrl}}/customers`\n\n### Method\n\n`POST`\n\n### Request Body\n\nThe request body must be in JSON format and should include the following parameters:\n\n- **name** (string): The full name of the customer.\n    \n- **email** (string): The email address of the customer.\n    \n\n#### Example Request\n\n``` json\n{\n  \"name\": \"John Doe\",\n  \"email\": \"john.doe@example.com\"\n}\n\n ```\n\n## Response\n\nUpon successful creation of a customer, the API will return a JSON object containing the following fields:\n\n- **customerId** (string): A unique identifier for the newly created customer.\n    \n- **name** (string): The name of the customer.\n    \n- **email** (string): The email address of the customer.\n    \n\n### Example Response\n\n``` json\n{\n  \"customerId\": \"12345\",\n  \"name\": \"John Doe\",\n  \"email\": \"john.doe@example.com\"\n}\n\n ```"
